  "releaseNotes": "2.0.0 — the first stable release of the 2.x line. The API is identical to\n            2.0.0-rc.1; what changed is the evidence behind it.\n\n            The release candidate ran in production for two working days across 1,029\n            Business Central calls with no BC-attributable failure and no rollback, and cut\n            Entra token round trips by roughly 93% — the singleton token provider fixing a\n            real 1.0 bug, where token state living on a transient typed client meant\n            re-authenticating far more often than necessary.\n\n            The behaviours 2.0 is built on are now measured against a real tenant rather than\n            asserted in documentation: server-driven paging follows a genuine @odata.nextLink\n            and returns every row exactly once; a kindless DateTime filters as UTC instead of\n            being shifted by the machine's timezone; $select is case-insensitive; native 'in'\n            needs $schemaversion=2.1; an over-length query string is answered 414.\n\n            Upgrading from 1.0 changes behaviour silently in places — paging, 204 on writes,\n            kindless DateTime filters, and the derived $select. Read the migration guide\n            before upgrading, even if the build is green:\n            https://github.com/KralGmbh/Dynamics365-BusinessCentral/blob/master/MIGRATION.md\n\n            Full changelog:\n            https://github.com/KralGmbh/Dynamics365-BusinessCentral/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md",
